course: dictionary
lesson: 1020
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Bony» can mean very thin, can describe food full of small bones, or can mean made of bone. The words around it show you which meaning the author wants.
explain: Look at the clues. «A bony old horse» means a very thin horse, because the horse is old and its bones show. «A bony fish» means a fish with lots of small bones, so you need to take care when eating it.
explain: Science texts use bony to mean made of bone. «The bony skull» is a skull made of bone. Always test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Bony has three main meanings: very thin, full of small bones (for food), and made of bone.
fact: Bony is an adjective, and it changes to bonier and boniest.
fact: «Bony fish» are fish with skeletons of bone, while sharks have cartilage instead.
fact: «A turtle's shell» is part of its skeleton, with bony plates grown together.
fact: «Ankylosaurus» was covered with bony plates in its skin.
exercise: «A bony old horse» was standing in the field. What does bony mean here? | Brightly coloured | Very loud and noisy | *Very thin, so the bones show | Covered in soft fur
exercise: «Be careful: the bony fish has many small bones.» What does bony describe? | A sad, grey sky | *Food, especially fish, with many small bones | A loud, shouting crowd | A person who is very tall
exercise: In «the bony skull», what is the skull made of? | Glass | *Bone | Water | Wool
test: «Sturgeon have five rows of bony plates along the body.» What do the bony plates mean? | *Plates made of bone | Small shiny stones | Rows of soft wool | Bright paint on the skin
test: «SuperCroc had a round bony bump at the tip of its snout, and nobody knows for sure what it was for.» What do scientists not know for sure? | *What the round bony bump was for | Why SuperCroc was so small | What colour its skin was | How fast SuperCroc could run
exam: «The bony fish made Sam careful when eating.» Which meaning fits best? | Covered in soft feathers | Very happy and fast | Made of glass | *Full of small bones, so needing care
